# Everything in this repo is consumed by Linux tooling even though it is usually edited on
# Windows: psql reads the SQL, bash runs the migration harness and the deploy scripts, and Vite
# builds the SPA. Checking those files out with CRLF is not cosmetic here:
#
#   * a carriage return reaching a psql \echo lands in the emitted env block as a trailing \r
#     inside a pasted user id, which fails far from where it was introduced;
#   * a CRLF shell script dies on its first line with "\r: command not found".
#
# Without this file, core.autocrlf=true (the Windows default, and the setting on this machine)
# rewrites every checkout to CRLF, and git warns on every commit that it is about to.
#
# text=auto still lets git sniff content, so the PNGs and WebP under public/ are detected as
# binary and left byte-for-byte alone.
* text=auto eol=lf
